## Owner Registration & `registrationDate` — Findings

The `POST /owners` flow is an OfficeFloor function chain wired by `owners.POST.yml`. Owner-creation functions live in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`) are **generated** from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (not present as source files).

### 1. Where `registrationDate` is set / defaulted (server-date default)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`
```java
13  public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
14      Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
15      if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
16          owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
17      }
18      built.set(owner);
19  }
```
This is the ONLY place the default is applied. It uses a plain `LocalDate.now()` with **no business-day / weekend / holiday rolling**. This is significant — see the test in section 5, which asserts the default must never be a Saturday or Sunday.

### 2. Membership number generation (year segment from registration date)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerMembershipNumber.java`
```java
17  public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
18      String yy = String.format(Locale.ROOT, "%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
19      owner.setMembershipNumber(owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + yy);
20  }
```
Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`). The `customerCode` prefix is assigned just before, in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` (format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, per-city sequence). Order in the chain: `assignCustomerCode` → `assignMembershipNumber`.

### 3. Daily create-limit enforcement (counting owners per day)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckOwnerDailyLimit.java`
```java
15  static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;
17  public void service(OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DailyOwnerLimitExceededException {
18      LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();
19      long registeredToday = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
20              .filter(existing -> today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))
21              .count();
22      if (registeredToday >= DAILY_LIMIT) {
23          throw new DailyOwnerLimitExceededException(
24                  DAILY_LIMIT + " or more owners have already been created today");
25      }
26  }
```
Supporting escalation (returns HTTP 429):
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java` (sends `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`)
- Wired by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.yml`

Note: the limit is counted against `registrationDate == LocalDate.now()`, using `findAll()` (soft-deleted owners are included unless filtered elsewhere). There is a parallel `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` / `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` set for per-city limits.

### 4. Owner entity/model, DTOs, and POST YAML
- Entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
  - `registrationDate` field: line 55-56 (`@Column(name = "registration_date") private LocalDate registrationDate;`); getter/setter lines 105-111.
  - `membershipNumber`: lines 61-62, 121-127. `customerCode`: 58-59. `namesakeCount`, `householdId`, derived `getMembershipTier()` (145-152) and `getLocality()` (154-165).
- Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` at line 29 (registrationDate mapped by name, no custom logic).
- DTO schema (generated source of `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`
  - `registrationDate` property: lines 2047-2054 ("When omitted on create it defaults to the server's current date" — no business-day mention here).
  - `membershipNumber`: lines 2110-2118. Note the DTO has a create-time `sharesHousehold` hint (2055-2063).
- POST wiring: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — full chain: `validate → normalizeEmail → normalizeAddress → normalize(telephone) → checkTelephoneUnique → checkHouseholdUnique → checkCityCapacity → checkDailyLimit → build → assignCustomerCode → assignMembershipNumber → assignHousehold → countNamesakes → save → respond`. Authorized via `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`.

### 5. Existing tests (registration date / membership / create-limit)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
```java
 9 /** business-day: the default registration date must fall on a business day (a weekend rolls
10  * forward to Monday). ... assert the invariant that holds
11  * every day: the default registrationDate is never a Saturday or Sunday. */
14  @Test
15  void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
16      int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
17      DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(fetchOwner(id).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
18      assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
19  }
```
This test expects business-day defaulting that the current `BuildOwner` does NOT implement (it would fail whenever the run date is a weekend).

Test harness base: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` contains the relevant helpers:
- `today()` line 110-112; `createMany(int n)` lines 181-187 ("all dated today — used to drive the per-day create-limit / bulk-signup rules").
- `fillCity(...)` lines 173-179 (per-city capacity).
- `HOLIDAYS` set lines 240-242 (2026 AU public holidays) and `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` roll-forward helper lines 267-274 — both anticipate business-day/holiday logic not yet present in `BuildOwner`.
- Comment lines 37-39 explicitly mention the "membership number, per-day cap, per-city cap" rules being count/quota based.
- `AuditLogCapture.java` also exists in that package (audit rules, not registration-specific).

### Key observation / likely gap
The spec artifacts (`AcceptanceTest.coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay`, `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`, `HOLIDAYS`) all assume the default `registrationDate` rolls weekends/holidays forward to the next business day, but `BuildOwner.java:16` sets a raw `LocalDate.now()` with no such rolling. No weekend/Saturday/Sunday/holiday/business-day logic exists anywhere in `src/main/java`.

